  "practice": [
    "Say ছ three times with a strong puff of air: chhô, chhô, chhô.",
    "Practice the vowel forms: ছ (chhô), ছা (chha), ছি (chhi), ছী (chhi, uncommon), ছু (chhu), ছূ (chhu, rare), ছে (chhe), ছৈ (chhoi, uncommon), ছো (chho), and ছৌ (chhou, uncommon).",
    "Read the combinations aloud: ছ + া = ছা as in ছাতা, ছ + ি = ছি as in ছিঁড়ে, ছ + ু = ছু as in ছুরি, ছ + ে = ছে as in ছেলে, and ছ + ো = ছো as in ছোট.",
    "Put your hand near your mouth and compare চ (ch, less air) with ছ (chh, a stronger puff of air).",
    "Use ছেলে, ছবি, ছোট, ছাতা, ছুটি, ছয়, ছাড়া, and ছায়া as quick reading anchors."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ছ is a Bangla consonant named chhô. Its sound is roughly chh, an aspirated version of চ with a stronger burst of air.",
    "চ and ছ are an important reading and pronunciation pair: চ is ch, while ছ is chh.",
    "Compare চা (cha, tea), চাল (chal, rice), and চোখ (chokh, eye) with ছাতা (chhata, umbrella), ছবি (chhobi, picture), ছেলে (chhele, boy), and ছোট (chhoto, small).",
    "Best words to memorize include ছেলে, ছবি, ছোট, ছয়, ছাড়া, ছাতা, ছুটি, ছাদ, ছায়া, ছাগল, ছুরি, ছাই, ছাপ, ছেঁড়া, ছোঁয়া, ছড়া, and ছাড়ো.",
